{{also|Schneiden}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|snīdan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*snīþaną||to cut}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*sneyt-||to cut}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|snijden||to cut, carve, intersect}}, {{cog|nds|snieden||to cut}}, dialectal {{cog|en|snithe||to cut}}, {{cog|sv|snida||to carve, engrave}}, {{cog|is|sníða||to trim, tailor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dn̩/|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-schneiden.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|schneidet|schnitt|geschnitten|past subjunctive=schnitte}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[cut]]; to [[carve]]; to [[slice]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[pare]]; to [[clip]]; to [[mow]]; to [[prune]]; to [[trim]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|driving|figuratively}} to cut (someone) off; to cut in on (someone)
# {{lb|de|transitive|film}} to [[edit]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|reflexive}} to [[intersect]]
#: ''Die beiden Geraden '''schneiden''' sich.'' — “Both streets intersect.”
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[cut]] (oneself)
# {{lb|de|reflexive|colloquial}} to [[delude]] (oneself); to become mistaken
# to [[avoid]] somebody (to cut someone)
